.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt PIDP11-STY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pidp11-sty
.Nd Teletype terminal emulator for the PiDP-11
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl aiv
.Op Fl c Ar class
.Op Fl f Ar font
.Op Fl g Ar geometry
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl T Ar title
.Op Fl t Ar title
.Op Fl w Ar windowid
.Op Fl e Ar command Op Ar arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is an X11 terminal emulator styled after a Teletype Model 33, based on
the simple terminal
.Xr st 1 .
It runs
.Ar command
attached to a pseudo-terminal
.Pq or a
.Ar line
device with
.Fl l ,
rendering output in its own window at the excruciating 10 characters
per second, accompanied by sampled Teletype clatter.
.Pp
The packaged desktop entry
.Pq Teletype
runs
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pidp11-sty bash pdp11
.Ed
.Pp
which opens the console of the simulated PDP-11
(see
.Xr pdp11 1 )
in the Teletype window.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Nm
accepts the usual
.Xr st 1
options; the ones most often needed are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar font
Render text with
.Ar font
(an X core font name).
.It Fl g Ar geometry
Set the initial window size and position,
.Ar CxR Ns + Ns Ar x Ns + Ns Ar y
in characters.
.It Fl T Ar title
Set the window title.
.It Fl e Ar command ...
Run
.Ar command
instead of the shell.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev DISPLAY
The X server to open the window on.
.It Ev SHELL
The shell to run when no
.Fl e
command is given.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pdp11 1 ,
.Xr vt05 1 ,
.Xr tek4010 1
